%% ARA — Resume Analysis Pipeline Workflow
%% Accurately reflecting Active Synchronous Execution & Target Async Decoupling
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User as Candidate / Recruiter
  participant Web as Next.js Web App
  participant API as FastAPI Gateway
  participant Disk as Server Disk (uploads/)
  participant Parser as Resume Parser (pypdf)
  participant LLM as Ollama LLM Service
  participant DB as PostgreSQL 18

  Note over User,Web: Active Pipeline Execution (Verified in Codebase)
  User->>Web: 1. Select Resume Document (PDF)
  Web->>API: 2. POST /api/v1/resumes/upload (Multipart)
  API->>Disk: 3. Stream & Persist File to uploads/
  API->>Parser: 4. Extract Text Content & Characters
  API->>DB: 5. Insert Resume (scoped to organization_id)
  API-->>Web: 6. Return 200 OK (resume_id, characters)
  
  Web->>API: 7. POST /api/v1/analysis/jobs (Trigger Analysis)
  API->>DB: 8. Insert AnalysisJob (status: pending)
  API->>LLM: 9. Prompt Ollama for Structured Extraction (Skills, ATS Score, Gaps)
  LLM-->>API: 10. Return Structured Analysis JSON
  API->>DB: 11. Insert AnalysisResult & Update Status -> COMPLETED
  API-->>Web: 12. Return Job Status & Analysis Payload
  Web-->>User: 13. Render Structured Skills, ATS Feedback & Recommendations

  Note over API,DB: Planned Target Architecture: ARQ Background Worker Queue & Direct S3 Presigned Uploads
